attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on the anchor.** Column 0, `mlaA`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.4% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.07 bits {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at column 1**, `yfdF`, carried by 42%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P}. Then columns 7 to 13, `yfcV` to `yfcO`, are [[fimbrial proteins]], carried by 30 to 81%, in a region of plasticity in 68 to 96% of calls {S4, Q}. A second branch of 4 families runs through columns 8 to 11, [[fimbrial proteins]], in 10 to 14% {S4.b8, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 88%, and hesitates less there, 0.17 against 0.29 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 8, `yfcU`, a fork column, 1.20 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in the `men` genes**, columns 75 to 79, [[succinyl hydroxy synthase]], carried by 41 to 73% {S6.c75-79, Q}. The last column is `menC`, in 41% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 91% of genes**, 0.25 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.91 against 0.14 bits, and names fewer genes, 62% against 96% {C}.

